# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accepted risks for the Trivy IaC scan gate.
#
# Every entry here is a finding the scanner is RIGHT about. The Wiz technical
# exercise requires these weaknesses on purpose; each one is documented with
# why it's accepted and what the production fix would be.
# Anything NOT listed here (HIGH/CRITICAL) fails the pipeline.
# The full list of findings, ignored ones included, is in the GitHub Security tab.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backup bucket: public read + public listing (required by the exercise) ---
# Fix: keep all four Block Public Access settings on; share backups via
# short-lived presigned URLs or cross-account access only.
AWS-0086
AWS-0087
AWS-0091
AWS-0093

# --- Backup bucket encrypted with SSE-S3, not a customer-managed KMS key ---
# A KMS key would make anonymous reads fail, breaking the required public access.
# Fix: SSE-KMS with a CMK, once the bucket is private.
AWS-0132

# --- MongoDB VM: SSH open to 0.0.0.0/0 (required by the exercise) ---
# Fix: no inbound SSH; use SSM Session Manager, or restrict 22 to a VPN/admin CIDR.
AWS-0107

# --- Unrestricted egress (MongoDB VM and EKS node security groups) ---
# Nodes and the VM need outbound HTTPS for packages, ECR pulls and S3 backups.
# Fix: VPC endpoints for ECR/S3/STS plus an egress proxy or firewall allowlist.
AWS-0104

# --- EKS API endpoint public and open to 0.0.0.0/0 (step 7 design trade-off) ---
# Lets GitHub-hosted runners deploy; every request still needs IAM auth plus an
# EKS access entry. Fix: private endpoint + self-hosted runner or GitOps (Argo CD).
AWS-0040
AWS-0041
